    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "070a5782_6f5a36d8",
        "filename": "src/dsp/dsp.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1249724
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-16T17:52:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we want this flag to support all these cases:\n1. Wasm (no SIMD)\n2. Wasm SIMD via SSE compat headers\n3. Wasm SIMD via intrinsics (dec_wasm)\n\nWEBP_USE_SIMD\u003dOFF will set WEBP_HAVE_WASM_SIMD\u003dOFF, so we will not use SIMD at all.\nWEBP_USE_SIMD\u003dON cannot distinguish between case 2 and 3 if we don\u0027t have WEBP_ENABLE_WASM_SIMD. Because in cpu.cmake, it tries -msimd128, and the compile check will succeed, so we always first hit case 3.",
      "parentUuid": "7123807c_640eca46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "ed665a15e895ac51b0cec8adcde52b095249dbd6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47d1353a_7a001cb6",
        "filename": "src/dsp/dsp.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002219
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-18T03:18:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think we want this flag to support all these cases:\n\u003e 1. Wasm (no SIMD)\n\u003e 2. Wasm SIMD via SSE compat headers\n\u003e 3. Wasm SIMD via intrinsics (dec_wasm)\n\u003e \n\u003e WEBP_USE_SIMD\u003dOFF will set WEBP_HAVE_WASM_SIMD\u003dOFF, so we will not use SIMD at all.\n\u003e WEBP_USE_SIMD\u003dON cannot distinguish between case 2 and 3 if we don\u0027t have WEBP_ENABLE_WASM_SIMD. Because in cpu.cmake, it tries -msimd128, and the compile check will succeed, so we always first hit case 3.\n\nso then we just need WEBP_HAVE_WASM_SIMD and a check on __wasm_simd128__ to make sure we can target it, kind of like we\u0027re doing for NEON. The USE in this case means targeting the architecture so the intrinsics can be built.",
      "parentUuid": "070a5782_6f5a36d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "ed665a15e895ac51b0cec8adcde52b095249dbd6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2196a04c_58ee131e",
        "filename": "src/dsp/dsp.h",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1249724
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-18T21:06:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that isn\u0027t enough because __wasm_simd128__ can mean either SSE compat headers or wasm simd intrinsics. Both require __wasm_simd128__, so if we check for that we can\u0027t differentiate which case it is. (i.e. __wasm_simd128__ just means we have SIMD support, and both the SSE headers and Wasm SIMD intrinsics require SIMD support).",
      "parentUuid": "47d1353a_7a001cb6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 62
      },
